# What each C11 machine of the `c11-mcu` gate costs a Cortex-M4 image, in bytes,
# and how far each figure may drift (docs/adr/0110, D3 item 2).
#
# Read by `scripts/gates/c11-mcu.sh`, which sources this file. The shape and the
# rule are the Rust lane's (`backends/rust/probes/nostd-footprint/footprint.budget`):
#
#   - Every figure is MEASURED, by the gate, with the toolchain named in
#     MEASURED_WITH, never estimated.
#   - A figure moves only by a commit that changes this file and says in its
#     message what the bytes bought. RE-PINNING IS A DECISION, NOT A CHORE.
#   - The gate fails on a figure outside its band in EITHER direction: a figure
#     that falls without a reason means the instrument stopped seeing.
#
# WHAT IS WEIGHED. For each machine, the `.text`, `.rodata`, `.data` and `.bss`
# of the objects compiled from what the generator wrote for it (its `.c`, and
# the units of what it imports), with the gate's flags (D3 item 1): the
# machine's own code and the runtime it pulls in, which is header-only and so
# compiled into those objects. Not weighed: the gate's startup, memory
# functions, seams, the scenario table and its runner, which are the test
# board's and not the machine's. The linked image's sections and the members of
# libgcc it pulls in are written to `target/c11-mcu/report.md` beside these.
# The codec, which no statechart imports yet, is weighed as the object of the
# program that writes and reads one value of it (`backends/c/mcu/codec_main.c`):
# its unit is header-only, so that object is where its code is.
#
# Each machine's figures are `<MACHINE>_TEXT`, `<MACHINE>_RODATA`,
# `<MACHINE>_DATA` and `<MACHINE>_BSS`, `<MACHINE>` its name in upper case.
#
# UNMEASURED. This entry holds no figure yet: the gate was written where no ARM
# compiler could run, and a guessed budget is the thing this file exists to
# refuse. The gate REFUSES TO PASS while any figure below is empty, and prints
# every figure it measured as the `NAME=value` lines to put here. The figures
# will be measured with Arm GNU Toolchain 13.2.rel1, the release
# scripts/install_arm_gnu_toolchain.sh pins and the gate runs (bx.toml's
# `[platform.linux.tools.arm-none-eabi-gcc]` on a build machine, the same script
# in c11-mcu.yml); the first run on such a machine measures them, and that
# commit sets TOLERANCE_BYTES too and says why the tolerance is what it is.

# The toolchain the figures are measured with, as `arm-none-eabi-gcc --version`
# prints its first line: Arm's build of the release the install script pins,
# which the gate refuses to run without. Printed beside the running one when a
# figure is out of its band, so a red that is only the toolchain says so. It is
# named before the figures are, so the commit that measures them cannot take
# them from another build.
MEASURED_WITH='arm-none-eabi-gcc (Arm GNU Toolchain 13.2.rel1 (Build arm-13.7)) 13.2.1 20231009'

# Drift allowed either way before the gate speaks, in bytes, for each figure.
TOLERANCE_BYTES=''

STATIC_COUNTER_TEXT=''
STATIC_COUNTER_RODATA=''
STATIC_COUNTER_DATA=''
STATIC_COUNTER_BSS=''

PLAIN_FOOTPRINT_PROBE_TEXT=''
PLAIN_FOOTPRINT_PROBE_RODATA=''
PLAIN_FOOTPRINT_PROBE_DATA=''
PLAIN_FOOTPRINT_PROBE_BSS=''

STATIC_MAP_TEXT=''
STATIC_MAP_RODATA=''
STATIC_MAP_DATA=''
STATIC_MAP_BSS=''

STATIC_MAP_TAKE_TEXT=''
STATIC_MAP_TAKE_RODATA=''
STATIC_MAP_TAKE_DATA=''
STATIC_MAP_TAKE_BSS=''

STATIC_STATE_ALGORITHM_TEXT=''
STATIC_STATE_ALGORITHM_RODATA=''
STATIC_STATE_ALGORITHM_DATA=''
STATIC_STATE_ALGORITHM_BSS=''

CODEC_CBOR_MAP_TEXT=''
CODEC_CBOR_MAP_RODATA=''
CODEC_CBOR_MAP_DATA=''
CODEC_CBOR_MAP_BSS=''
